  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 250 AM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nWednesday... A blocked rather messy upper air pattern continues to \nunfold acrs much of the CONUS, with both upper and sfc ridging off \nthat complex taking over the local area by mid week. This should \nmake for a mainly dry day for Wed, but several models are sloshing \nclouds and moisture back westward acrs the DVN CWA in easterly low \nto mid level flow under H75 MB inversion. Thus there may be more \nclouds than earlier expected for a mostly cloudy day, and a few \nsolutions break out isolated diurnal light showers Wed afternoon. \nWill keep it dry for now but increase the cloud cover from the \nloaded blend. If the clouds materialize, the loaded mid to high 60s \nfor high temps may be a bit optimistic.\n\nThursday and Friday...The latest Ensembles and upper jet trends \ncontinue to suggest that some upper wave/trof energy to try and \nundercut mid CONUS omega bloc and spill some showers into the area \nfrom the west Thursday or Thursday evening. Will bank on upper ridge \naxis having it's precip corrosive effect and erode it before it \nget's into the area, but we may have to deal with at least some \ndebris clouds moving in from the west making for not the most \nsunniest of days. High temps may gain be hindered some by this from \ntheir potentail of upper 60s to near 70. Upper trof battle with \nongoing omega bloc ridge will make for a showery northern plains and \nMO RVR Valley Friday, but again will bank on the ridge placement \nindicated by the latest medium range ensembles to keep this action \nat bay off to the west of the local fcst area through Friday night.\n\nSaturday through Monday...Some signs in the longer range of the \nomega ridge breaking down enough to allow the upper trof to sweep in \nand produce some showers in the area later Saturday or Saturday night \nif even in a decaying fashion. But again associated cloud cover may \nkeep temps down Saturday, before re-amplifying upper ridge allows \nfor drying and rebounding thicknesses for a warm up to a bit above \nnormal Sunday and especially by next Monday.",
